# Security and compliance

Treat every lead submission as untrusted. Validate with a schema, then rate-limit by IP and phone before writing a row. Reject the submission when the hidden honeypot is filled. Store the consent text, timestamp, page URL, and whether SMS and calls were allowed.

## Boundaries

- Admin pages check the session inside the data layer. Hiding a link is not authorization.
- Verify Twilio and Resend webhook signatures before updating a lead. Compare secrets in constant time.
- Secrets stay in environment variables. Never print a full phone number or message body in client logs.

## Claims the site must not make

- Do not promise that a foreclosure stops immediately, that credit is repaired, or that an offer matches a listed price.
- Take-over-payments copy must say the loan can stay in the seller's name and that a missed payment can still affect their credit.
- A lawyer reviews foreclosure timelines and takeover language before they ship.

